'''''Paleohoplias''''' is an [[extinct]] [[genus]] of freshwater [[Characiformes|characin]] fish in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Erythrinidae]] found in [[Brazil]], [[South America]]. Two species are known.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Decat |first=Bernardo |last2=Aguilera |first2=Orangel |last3=Costa da Silva |first3=Rafael |last4=Oliveira de Araújo |first4=Olga |last5=De Gracia |first5=Carlos |last6=Tadeu Lopes |first6=Ricardo |date=2026-04-15 |title=Fossil record and paleogeography of Erythrinidae (Characiformes): new fossil evidence of Paleohoplias from the Solimões Formation |url=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S089598112600009X |journal=Journal of South American Earth Sciences |volume=174 |article-number=105957 |doi=10.1016/j.jsames.2026.105957 |issn=0895-9811|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

== Taxonomy ==
The [[type species]] †'''''Paleohoplias assisbrasiliensis''''' <small>Bocquentin & Negri, 2003</small> was [[scientific description|described]] in 2003, and was found in the [[Solimões Formation]] in the [[State of Acre, Brazil]], dating to the [[Huayquerian|Huayqueriense]]-[[Montehermosan|Montehermoseuse]] ([[Late Miocene]]-[[Pliocene]]) age.<ref name="Gayet2003" /> A second species, †'''''Paleohoplias amazonensis''''' <small>Decat ''et al'', 2026</small> was described from the same formation in 2026.<ref name=":0" />

==Etymology==
The generic name ''Paleohoplias'' comes from the Greek ''palaios'', which means "old", and ''[[hoplias]]'', which is a closely related genus of fish in the same [[Family (taxonomy)|family]], [[Erythrinidae]]. The species name ''assisbrasiliensis'' is in reference to the city of [[Assis Brasil]], which is near the [[type locality (biology)|type locality]].<ref name="Gayet2003"/>

==Classification==
''Paleohoplias'' is one of four genera within the family Erythrinidae, and the only extinct genus.<ref name="Blanco2010">{{cite journal |last1=Blanco |first1=Daniel Rodrigues |last2=Lui |first2=Roberto Laridondo |last3=Bertollo |first3=Luiz Antonio Carlos |last4=Margarido |first4=Vladimir Pavan |last5=Moreira Filho |first5=Orlando |title=Karyotypic diversity between allopatric populations of the group ''Hoplias malabaricus'' (Characiformes: Erythrinidae): evolutionary and biogeographic considerations |journal=[[Neotropical Ichthyology]] |date=2010 |volume=8 |issue=2 |pages=361-368 |doi=10.1590/S1679-62252010000200015 |doi-access=free }}</ref> It is most closely related to the genus ''[[Hoplias]]''.<ref name="Gayet2003"/>

